json.library/JsonAdd                                      json.library/JsonAdd

   NAME
        JsonAdd -- Put a node into an object or array (0.1).

   SYNOPSIS
        ok = JsonAdd(parent, name, node)
        D0          A0      A1    A2

        LONG JsonAdd(JsonNode *, CONST_STRPTR, JsonNode *);

   FUNCTION
        Adds node as the last member of parent. In an object it needs a
        name (UTF-8; a byte that is not UTF-8 is taken as Latin-1); a
        member of that name already there is replaced. In an array the
        name is ignored (pass NULL).

   INPUTS
        parent - an object or array
        name   - the member's name (objects), or NULL
        node   - from JsonNew...(), or taken out with JsonRemove()

   RESULT
        ok - TRUE, or FALSE: node NULL, already in a tree, from another
             document, parent not an object or array (or no name for an
             object), or node is parent or holds it

        Notes: Since a failed JsonNew...() is NULL and JsonAdd() refuses
        NULL, JsonAdd(o, "x", JsonNewInt(doc, 5)) needs no checks.

   SEE ALSO
        JsonRemove](#jsonremove), JsonSetRoot


json.library/JsonAt                                        json.library/JsonAt

   NAME
        JsonAt -- An array's item by number (0.1).

   SYNOPSIS
        node = JsonAt(array, index)
        D0            A0     D0

        JsonNode *JsonAt(JsonNode *, LONG);

   FUNCTION
        Returns the item at index, counting from 0; a negative index
        counts from the end (-1 is the last).

   INPUTS
        array - an array
        index - which item

   RESULT
        node - the item, or NULL (not an array, or no such item)

        Notes: It walks from the start: in a loop over a big array use
        JsonFirst() and JsonNext().

   SEE ALSO
        JsonFirst](#jsonfirst), JsonFind


