json.library/JsonFind                                    json.library/JsonFind

   NAME
        JsonFind -- A node by path (0.1).

   SYNOPSIS
        node = JsonFind(start, path)
        D0              A0     A1

        JsonNode *JsonFind(JsonNode *, CONST_STRPTR);

   FUNCTION
        Follows a path from start: names joined by dots, [n] for an
        array's n-th item (from 0, negative from the end), ["name"] for a
        name with dots or brackets (\" and \\ inside). An empty path is
        start itself.

   INPUTS
        start - where the path begins (usually JsonRoot(doc))
        path  - like "weather.days[0].temp" (UTF-8)

   RESULT
        node - what the path leads to, or NULL

   SEE ALSO
        JsonGet](#jsonget), JsonAt


json.library/JsonFirst                                  json.library/JsonFirst

   NAME
        JsonFirst -- The first member (0.1).

   SYNOPSIS
        member = JsonFirst(node)
        D0                A0

        JsonNode *JsonFirst(JsonNode *);

   FUNCTION
        Returns the first member of an object or array; JsonNext() gives
        the rest.

   INPUTS
        node - an object or array

   RESULT
        member - the first member, or NULL (empty, or not an object or array)

        Notes: for (m = JsonFirst(o); m; m = JsonNext(m)) ...

   SEE ALSO
        JsonNext](#jsonnext), JsonName


json.library/JsonFree                                    json.library/JsonFree

   NAME
        JsonFree -- Free a document (0.1).

   SYNOPSIS
        JsonFree(doc)
                 A0

        VOID JsonFree(JsonDoc *);

   FUNCTION
        Frees the document and every node and string in it. Nothing from
        it may be used afterwards.

   INPUTS
        doc - from JsonParse(), JsonLoad() or JsonNewDoc(); NULL is safe

   SEE ALSO
        JsonParse](#jsonparse), JsonNewDoc


json.library/JsonGet                                      json.library/JsonGet

   NAME
        JsonGet -- An object's member by name (0.1).

   SYNOPSIS
        node = JsonGet(object, name)
        D0             A0      A1

        JsonNode *JsonGet(JsonNode *, CONST_STRPTR);

   FUNCTION
        Returns the member called name. If the name is there more than
        once, the last one (as JavaScript does).

   INPUTS
        object - an object
        name   - the name, UTF-8

   RESULT
        node - the member, or NULL

   SEE ALSO
        JsonFind](#jsonfind), JsonAt


json.library/JsonInt                                      json.library/JsonInt

   NAME
        JsonInt -- A number as a whole number (0.1).

   SYNOPSIS
        value = JsonInt(node, def)
        D0              A0    D0

        LONG JsonInt(JsonNode *, LONG);

   FUNCTION
        Returns the number rounded to the nearest whole number (halves
        away from zero: 8.5 is 9, -8.5 is -9), kept between -2147483648
        and 2147483647. A string that is exactly a JSON number ("8.5")
        counts as that number.

   INPUTS
        node - a number
        def  - what to return for anything else

   RESULT
        value - the number, or def

   SEE ALSO
        JsonScaled](#jsonscaled), JsonNumText


json.library/JsonLatin1                                json.library/JsonLatin1

   NAME
        JsonLatin1 -- A string as Amiga text (0.1).

   SYNOPSIS
        length = JsonLatin1(node, buf, size)
        D0                  A0    A1   D0

        LONG JsonLatin1(JsonNode *, STRPTR, LONG);

   FUNCTION
        Copies a string (or a number's text) into buf as Latin-1, ended
        with a 0. Characters Latin-1 does not have become the nearest it
        has (L as L, EUR as E, curly quotes as ", dashes as -), else ?.

   INPUTS
        node - a string or number
        buf  - where to put it; NULL only measures
        size - buf's size, the 0 included

   RESULT
        length - the whole text's length, even if buf was too small;
                 -1 if node is not a string or number (buf gets "")

        Notes: JsonLatin1(n, NULL, 0) + 1 is the buffer size needed.

   SEE ALSO
        JsonString](#jsonstring), JsonNewString


json.library/JsonLength                                json.library/JsonLength

   NAME
        JsonLength -- A string's length (0.1).

   SYNOPSIS
        length = JsonLength(node)
        D0                  A0

        LONG JsonLength(JsonNode *);

   FUNCTION
        Returns the length in bytes (UTF-8) of a string, or of a number's
        text.

   INPUTS
        node - a string or number

   RESULT
        length - the bytes, or 0 for anything else

        Notes: A string can hold a 0 byte (\u0000 in the JSON):
        JsonString() stops there, JsonLength() does not.

   SEE ALSO
        JsonString](#jsonstring)


json.library/JsonLoad                                    json.library/JsonLoad

   NAME
        JsonLoad -- Read a JSON file (0.1).

   SYNOPSIS
        doc = JsonLoad(name, flags, err)
        D0            A0    D0     A1

        JsonDoc *JsonLoad(CONST_STRPTR, ULONG, struct JsonError *);

   FUNCTION
        Reads a whole file (or pipe) and reads it as JsonParse() does.

   INPUTS
        name  - the file
        flags - as JsonParse()
        err   - filled in when it fails; may be NULL

   RESULT
        doc - the document, or NULL (Message: "cannot open the file",
              "cannot read the file", "out of memory", or what was
              wrong with the JSON)

   SEE ALSO
        JsonParse](#jsonparse), JsonWriteFH


