json.library/JsonScaled                                json.library/JsonScaled

   NAME
        JsonScaled -- A number as fixed point (0.1).

   SYNOPSIS
        value = JsonScaled(node, places, def)
        D0                 A0    D0      D1

        LONG JsonScaled(JsonNode *, LONG, LONG);

   FUNCTION
        Returns the number times 10 to the power places, rounded to the
        nearest whole number (halves away from zero) and kept within a
        LONG: 8.25 with 2 places is 825, with 1 place 83. A string that is
        exactly a JSON number counts as that number.

   INPUTS
        node   - a number
        places - 0 to 9
        def    - what to return for anything else (or places out of range)

   RESULT
        value - the scaled number, or def

   SEE ALSO
        JsonInt](#jsonint), JsonNumText


json.library/JsonSetRoot                              json.library/JsonSetRoot

   NAME
        JsonSetRoot -- Set a document's top value (0.1).

   SYNOPSIS
        JsonSetRoot(doc, node)
                    A0   A1

        VOID JsonSetRoot(JsonDoc *, JsonNode *);

   FUNCTION
        Makes node the document's top value. The old one (if any) stays in
        the document, out of the tree.

   INPUTS
        doc  - the document
        node - a node of doc that is in no object or array; NULL empties it

   SEE ALSO
        JsonRoot](#jsonroot), JsonNewDoc


json.library/JsonString                                json.library/JsonString

   NAME
        JsonString -- A string's text (0.1).

   SYNOPSIS
        text = JsonString(node)
        D0                A0

        CONST_STRPTR JsonString(JsonNode *);

   FUNCTION
        Returns a string's text, UTF-8, ended with a 0 (read-only, valid
